{"ts":"2026-08-04T09:30:07.005Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"ecc9554d11d78abfd35454a3","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Design a deterministic execution-context contract for linked tests. Detect commands that use scripts/run-tests.mjs or self-contained benchmark fixtures; do not inject an empty schema PM_PATH when it changes their meaning, or require and persist an explicit per-test context mode with a clear add-time diagnostic. The output must show the effective context before execution and recommend the correct bounded retry. Preserve the rule that tests never read or write real repository PM data."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-e97jyf"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Linked-test schema context changes non-PM repository checks, so commands that pass directly fail when recorded and run through pm test"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The 2026-08-04 audit linked existing sandbox-safe repository commands to its PM plan. The focused merge suite passed directly at 120/120, but pm test default schema context failed 1/120 because validate_merge_driver_configuration warnings appeared only under the linked sandbox. The 10k scale gate passed directly, but failed under the same inherited PM_PATH context with token and latency threshold changes. Build/typecheck and published-release verification passed in both contexts. The runner correctly isolates tracker mutations, but it silently changes semantics for non-PM commands that already create their own fixtures."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-04T09:30:07.005Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-04T09:30:07.005Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Per-test execution context is explicit, persisted, and visible before command execution.; Self-sandboxing repository test and benchmark commands have parity between direct and linked execution without access to real tracker data.; Merge and scale regression fixtures cover schema, tracker-copy, and self-sandboxing modes with guided recovery.; The runner distinguishes assertion failure caused by execution context from an actual product gate regression."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-92if"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm CLI 2026.8.4, linked-test default pm_context_mode=schema"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Link the focused merge suite and pnpm benchmark:scale:check to a PM item, run pm test <id> --run --progress, then run the same commands directly through scripts/run-tests.mjs and pnpm."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Sandbox-safe commands produce the same assertions and performance contract directly and through pm test, with explicit context metadata where semantic differences are intentional."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Direct merge tests pass 120/120 and direct scale gate passes; linked schema context produces merge-driver configuration warnings and scale token/latency threshold failures."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Agents cannot trust the canonical linked-test evidence loop and may misclassify orchestration-context failures as product regressions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":